the wind turbines you see behind me are  part of one of the largest wind farms in  europe they're also the reason why there  aren't any reindeer roaming the area of  fusion anymore reindeer used to roam  this vast area of mid-norway only a few  years back  now the animals are long gone  instead  one of europe's biggest wind power  plants is dominating the area of fusion  but the wind powered development has  made it almost impossible for the  indigenous sami people to hurt reindeer  in an unexpected ruling late last year  norway's supreme court stated that the  wind turbines was built on permits that  are no longer valid the reason is that  the permits breaches the sami people's  right to exercise its culture  [Music]  [Music]  and several ngos now demand that the  wind plant consisting of  151 wind turbines  is being dismantled so the animals can  return  so far  nothing has happened  the turbines are still in operation and  norway's government hasn't offered a  solution yet on one hand the government  has said that it will be a world leader  when it comes to indigenous people's  rights on the other hand the nation  needs renewable energy and the  government could also be held  responsible for the wind company's loss  if the turbines are to be torn down  norway's new government has described  this as one of the most difficult cases  in several years prime minister yunus  garciarde said in february that he  understand the sami's frustration  but that there is nothing in the ruling  that implies that the turbines has to be  dismantled as the government is looking  for solutions nobody knows if the  reindeer will be able to return to the  area where they've been winter grazing  for hundreds of years
 

